  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="9233-3690-cc10-4e32" name="Barbarian Army List - List Notes" publicationId="556c-7119-7234-b625" hidden="false">
      <description>BARBARIAN ARMY LIST (WAB 2nd Edition, pp.182-189)
Covers Gallic, British and Germanic armies c.500 BC-500 AD. Characters up to 1/3 of points; Warriors at least 1/3; Cavalry and Chariots up to 1/3; Supporting Infantry up to 1/3.
Warbands of at least 5 models (chariots 3). Standard bearer, musician, leader +5 each. Supporting Infantry: no maximum size.
ADAPTING THE LIST (p.189; not enforced):
Gauls: may field warriors in open order.
Germans: no chariots or mountain tribesmen; noble cavalry may not take light armour but are Fearsome; noble cavalry and warriors may be stubborn +2/model; warriors may take thrusting spears +1 (such troops must be upgraded to stubborn); non-fanatic warriors may take throwing spears +2.
Dacians: no chariots; any warriors may be replaced by Mountain Tribesmen; warriors and mountain tribesmen may take halberds +2 per model; mountain tribesmen may have a bow +2 if no falx.
Ancient Britons: no noble cavalry or bows; chariots come from the warrior points allowance, one per eight infantry warriors; chariots within 6" of friendly light cavalry cannot be targeted by enemy missile fire.</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
</catalogue>
